Hey everyone,

I just commited (if I let nothing slip) all the changes regarding your comments.

@maryamsulemani97 The doc I copied is the one from the executable from Meilisearch. It’s the doc printed when you launch the application with the `--help` flag. I took your comments into consideration and applied them on the help as well.

@curquiza I reworked the config.toml file, I hope this one is better! I enhanced the error management and print the imported file as requested. I also forced the file to be snake_case and an error will now be raised if an unknown key is used.

@Kerollmops The destructuration is indeed a very neat approach, thanks !! As for the readability of the config.toml I agree this isn’t the easiest file to read. However, some flags are computed at runtime when defaulted so I’m not quite sure if uncommenting them is the best approach. Please let me know what’s your point of view regarding this !

I hope this iteration is better than the previous one. I stay available if you have remarks and if further changes are requested ! 🙂
